<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qutuz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1260">1260</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Qutuz</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qutuz was a sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> in 1259–1260. With the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> army that defeated a Mongol force under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kitbuqa">Kitbuqa</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Ain Jalut</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galilee">Galilee</a> in 1260. The battle set a decisive limit to the westward expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, and Qutuz was killed shortly afterwards.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qutuz.jpg" alt="Qutuz" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SoultanOmar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%B5%D9%88%D8%B1%D8%A9_%D8%AA%D9%85%D8%AB%D8%A7%D9%84_%D8%B3%D9%8A%D9%81_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AF%D9%8A%D9%86_%D9%82%D8%B7%D8%B2_crop.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
